id: pm-46hpx8
title: "GH-1158: Windows Node 24 nightly receipt fixture derives a root-relative expectation from a drive-qualified path"
description: "Nightly Validation run 33304991848 failed only on windows-latest / Node 24 because the npm 12 keyed-receipt regression fixture compares the production drive-qualified tarball path against path.join('/tmp/pack', 'beta.tgz'), which is root-relative on Windows. The product selection behavior succeeded; the supposedly cross-platform acceptance test encoded a POSIX root and made the nightly release signal red."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-30T14:39:02.916Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T16:32:31.361Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T16:32:30.751Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T16:32:30.751Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: The fixture derives expected package tarballs from the same explicit temporary root on every platform without weakening the production assertion; A focused regression passes locally and the hosted Windows Node 24 matrix is green; GitHub issue 1158 links this canonical item and the release-health lineage records the terminal result
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Replaced the POSIX-rooted receipt expectation with one derived from the same path.resolve pack root as the production tarball inputs; exact-head hosted Windows Node 24 CI now passes.
expected_result: The keyed npm receipt fixture derives all expected tarball paths from one platform-qualified temporary root and the Windows Node 24 matrix passes.
actual_result: "Focused and full exact-coverage suites pass locally, and PR #1160 exact head 7238f87ac passed CI Windows regression (Node 24) job 99286005978 in run 33322150088."
