comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T14:39:02.916Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status searches for run 33304991848 and the exact Nightly Validation Windows Node 24 wording found no item for GH-1158. Historical pm-gh1075, pm-lt6n, pm-zno2iu, pm-v3umtp, pm-wr8utz, and pm-j668gl own distinct prior Windows failures; this item records the new drive-qualified npm-receipt fixture mismatch."
  "2026-08-30T15:28:05.892Z","harness:codex","Local evidence: tests/unit/regressions/context-integrity-recovery.spec.ts passes in the focused suite and the complete 8,144-test coverage run at exact 100/100/100/100. The expected beta tarball now derives from the same path.resolve pack root as the production input. Item remains in progress until the PR's hosted Windows Node 24 job is terminal green."
  "2026-08-30T15:39:47.301Z","harness:codex","Delivery review: commit b031cd694 and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1160 carry the portable path fixture. This item remains in progress pending the PR Windows Node 24 hosted result."
  "2026-08-30T16:32:29.499Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance: PR #1160 exact head 7238f87ac passed every terminal check. Windows regression (Node 24) succeeded in CI run 33322150088, job 99286005978: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/33322150088/job/99286005978. Greptile reported 5/5 and no blocking failure; CodeRabbit was retriggered but its provider quota prevented a fresh full review within the bounded window, which is recorded as a limitation rather than approval."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T16:32:30.085Z","harness:codex",Cross-platform receipt fixtures must derive expectations from the same platform-qualified root used to build inputs; absolute-looking POSIX literals become drive-relative or root-relative on Windows and can invalidate release health without exercising a product defect.
